For a Monk (at one chance in three, significantly
the most likely role to be able to cast protection
in the very early game), the only metal armor
you're very likely to have at that point is a +0
orcish helm -- and you start with a robe, which
helps to offset it, and your base spellcasting
penalty is very reasonable as well, so the
chance of casting a low-level spell without
shifting armor around are fairly reasonable
in most cases.

The chance of being able to cast it three
times after you see the monster before it
attacks you are somewhat lower.  In my
admittedly limited experience, it tends to
go something more like this:

