I can now add prayer to my list of options,
because I'm almost out of hitpoints.  In
practice, however, what I'm going to do at
this point is displace Griff and flee back
toward the up stairs without delay.

My conclusion, prior to this thread, was
that casting protection when an enemy is
close like this is a pointless and potentially
deadly waste of precious time that ought to
be used either to fight or else to flee.  (The
door-closing option can be considered a
specific way of doing the latter.)

If the enemy is just a few tiles farther away,
I can cast undisturbed, but then the enemy
will invariably wander away, and I usually
won't find it before the protection wears off.


